### Pillar 4: Dynamic Risk Scaling (Kelly Criterion) 🎯

**My Suggestion**

Replace static position sizing with the **Kelly Criterion** — the mathematically optimal bet size:

```
Kelly % = (Win_Rate / Loss_Ratio) - ((1 - Win_Rate) / Win_Ratio)

Practical: Use Half-Kelly (50% of Kelly) for safety
```

**Why This Matters**:
- Current system uses fixed 7-15% position sizes regardless of edge quality
- Kelly sizes bets proportionally to edge strength
- A strategy with 70% win rate and 2:1 R:R gets a larger allocation than one with 55% win rate and 1.5:1 R:R

**Integration**:
- Compute Kelly % from rolling 30-trade statistics per strategy
- Cap at Half-Kelly for safety (institutional standard)
- Floor at 3% minimum (your current minimum)
- Update every 24 hours (not per-trade, to avoid overfitting)

